[38;5;231m⏺[39m This one's a one-line change, but it's a session lifetime, so I want your explicit go-ahead before I touch it.

  [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m has [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m. Going to 480 (8 hours) means a stolen or abandoned session stays valid
  16× longer — a session hijacked from a shared or unlocked machine, or a leaked session token, remains usable for a
  full working day instead of half an hour. [38;5;153mserver.js:3[39m reads the value directly, so the change takes effect everywhere
  sessions expire.

  If that's the intent, say go and I'll set it to 480. Worth knowing:

  - If the goal is "users shouldn't get logged out mid-work," a sliding/idle timeout (30 min of inactivity, refreshed on
